cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Molao: a decentralized commons of case law"
message: >-
  If you refer to Molao in research, teaching or a report, please cite it using
  these metadata. Cite the version you actually used — the project is early and
  changes substantially between versions.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Molao contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vul-os/molao"
url: "https://vulos.org/projects/molao/"
abstract: >-
  Molao is a free, decentralized commons of case law: a corpus of judgments
  identified by the BLAKE3 hash of their canonical text, a citation graph over
  them derived by a pinned deterministic extractor and therefore verifiable by
  recomputation, and a single offline-first binary that serves both. Releases
  are threshold-signed by a quorum of independent organisations rather than
  published by one operator; a threshold below two is refused in code.
  Jurisdictions are data, not code — court codes, hierarchy tiers and
  law-report series load from region-profile files at run time. Molao is
  infrastructure any jurisdiction can stand up for its own corpus, in the
  tradition of the Free Access to Law Movement.
keywords:
  - legal informatics
  - case law
  - free access to law
  - citation analysis
  - citator
  - content addressing
  - threshold signatures
  - decentralization
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
